From da58dfb31f05ebc9b4540e5b0a4be40292a2cea0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jesse Farmer <jesse@20bits.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 06:08:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Route scaled gradient fills through the glyph atlas

Repeat the fills-only atlas experiment on current #389 so its quality and
cost can be compared with the outline fix on the same upstream baseline.
Use the residual transform for glyph quads and the original canvas transform
for paint coordinates. Keep gradient and image strokes on outlines so their
join and dash settings are retained.

Update the old routing assertions, keep the outline tests above the atlas
size limit, and check gradient/image paint matrices at exact and residual
scales. Validation: 564 tests pass with wgpu; all 247 library tests pass with
wgpu and swash. cargo fmt --check passes.
